ev) played Pair 5s, which is a low block. If I pass, the Landlord (Next) can easily beat this with a medium pair like 9s or Jacks. I have a strong hand with pairs 7, 8, 10, Q, 2, and the Red Joker.\n\nReason: Playing Pair Q is the optimal move. It is high enough to block medium pairs (preventing the Landlord from sliding in a J or 10 pair) and forces the Landlord to use high-value cards (Kings, Aces, or 2s) to proceed. Playing 22 is unnecessary overkill for a pair of 5s, and playing 77 or 88 is too low and might help the Landlord get rid of small cards. Playing QQ applies the right amount of pressure while keeping my 22 and Red Joker for later control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠Q", "♥Q"]}'}
